Description: Share your Linux screen as a virtual webcam (CLI + GTK4 GUI)
 LinuxShare captures your screen (or a selected window on X11) and streams
 it into a v4l2loopback virtual camera device. The virtual camera can then
 be selected as a webcam inside Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Slack, Google Meet
 and any other application that reads a V4L2 device.
 .
 It supports both X11 (via ffmpeg x11grab) and Wayland (via
 xdg-desktop-portal + PipeWire) sessions, and ships both a command line
 tool (linuxshare-cli) and a GTK4 graphical application (linuxshare-gui).
